NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tanstack Form doesn't cause re-renders when interacting with the form. So, you might find yourself trying to use a form or field state value without success."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you would like to access reactive values, you will need to subscribe to them using one of two methods: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" or the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" component."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some uses for these subscriptions are rendering up-to-date field values, determining what to render based on a condition, or using field values inside the logic of your component."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For situations where you want to \"react\" to triggers, check out the "},{"type":"link","href":"./listeners.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"listener"}]},{"type":"text","value":" API."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"useselector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useSelector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/preact-form"},{"type":"text","value":" when you need form values inside component logic."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useSelector } from '@tanstack/preact-form'\n\nconst firstName = useSelector(form.store, (state) => state.values.firstName)\nconst errors = useSelector(form.store, (state) => state.errorMap)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useStore"},{"type":"text","value":" is still exported but deprecated; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" with the same arguments."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-subscribe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"form.Subscribe"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" component is best suited when you need to react to something within the UI of your component. For example, showing or hiding UI based on the value of a form field."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.Subscribe\n  selector={(state) => state.values.firstName}\n  children={(firstName) => (\n    <form.Field>\n      {(field) => (\n        <input\n          name=\"lastName\"\n          value={field.state.lastName}\n          onInput={field.handleChange}\n        />\n      )}\n    </form.Field>\n  )}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" component doesn't trigger component-level re-renders. Anytime the value subscribed to changes, only the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" component re-renders."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The choice between whether to use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" mainly boils down to your use case. If you're aiming for direct UI updates based on form state, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" for its optimization perks. And if you need the reactivity within the logic, then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" is the better choice."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"useselector","text":"useSelector","level":2},{"id":"form-subscribe","text":"form.Subscribe","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanstack Form doesn't cause re-renders when interacting with the form. So, you might find yourself trying to use a form or field state value without success.\n\nIf you would like to access reactive values, you will need to subscribe to them using one of two methods: `useSelector` or the `form.Subscribe` component.\n\nSome uses for these subscriptions are rendering up-to-date field values, determining what to render based on a condition, or using field values inside the logic of your component.\n\n> For situations where you want to \"react\" to triggers, check out the [listener](./listeners.md) API.\n\n## useSelector\n\nImport `useSelector` from `@tanstack/preact-form` when you need form values inside component logic.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/preact-form'\n\nconst firstName = useSelector(form.store, (state) => state.values.firstName)\nconst errors = useSelector(form.store, (state) => state.errorMap)\n```\n\n> **Migration:** `useStore` is still exported but deprecated; use `useSelector` with the same arguments.\n\n## form.Subscribe\n\nThe `form.Subscribe` component is best suited when you need to react to something within the UI of your component. For example, showing or hiding UI based on the value of a form field.\n\n```tsx\n<form.Subscribe\n  selector={(state) => state.values.firstName}\n  children={(firstName) => (\n    <form.Field>\n      {(field) => (\n        <input\n          name=\"lastName\"\n          value={field.state.lastName}\n          onInput={field.handleChange}\n        />\n      )}\n    </form.Field>\n  )}\n/>\n```\n\n> The `form.Subscribe` component doesn't trigger component-level re-renders. Anytime the value subscribed to changes, only the `form.Subscribe` component re-renders.\n\nThe choice between whether to use `useSelector` or `form.Subscribe` mainly boils down to your use case. If you're aiming for direct UI updates based on form state, use `form.Subscribe` for its optimization perks. And if you need the reactivity within the logic, then `useSelector` is the better choice.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: reactivity\ntitle: Reactivity\n---\n\nTanstack Form doesn't cause re-renders when interacting with the form. So, you might find yourself trying to use a form or field state value without success.\n\nIf you would like to access reactive values, you will need to subscribe to them using one of two methods: `useSelector` or the `form.Subscribe` component.\n\nSome uses for these subscriptions are rendering up-to-date field values, determining what to render based on a condition, or using field values inside the logic of your component.\n\n> For situations where you want to \"react\" to triggers, check out the [listener](./listeners.md) API.\n\n## useSelector\n\nImport `useSelector` from `@tanstack/preact-form` when you need form values inside component logic.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/preact-form'\n\nconst firstName = useSelector(form.store, (state) => state.values.firstName)\nconst errors = useSelector(form.store, (state) => state.errorMap)\n```\n\n> **Migration:** `useStore` is still exported but deprecated; use `useSelector` with the same arguments.\n\n## form.Subscribe\n\nThe `form.Subscribe` component is best suited when you need to react to something within the UI of your component. For example, showing or hiding UI based on the value of a form field.\n\n```tsx\n<form.Subscribe\n  selector={(state) => state.values.firstName}\n  children={(firstName) => (\n    <form.Field>\n      {(field) => (\n        <input\n          name=\"lastName\"\n          value={field.state.lastName}\n          onInput={field.handleChange}\n        />\n      )}\n    </form.Field>\n  )}\n/>\n```\n\n> The `form.Subscribe` component doesn't trigger component-level re-renders. Anytime the value subscribed to changes, only the `form.Subscribe` component re-renders.\n\nThe choice between whether to use `useSelector` or `form.Subscribe` mainly boils down to your use case. If you're aiming for direct UI updates based on form state, use `form.Subscribe` for its optimization perks. And if you need the reactivity within the logic, then `useSelector` is the better choice.\n"}
